{
 "id": "2026-10-26-ph-dilute-acid",
 "topic": "pH of 10^-8 M HCl is 6.98, not 8 (water autoionization, charge balance)",
 "subject": "chemistry",
 "hook_type": "exam pain",
 "caption": "The shortcut pH = -log10(c) gives 8 for 10^-8 M HCl, which is basic and impossible. Include water's own ions (Kw = 1e-14 at 25 C) and a charge balance, solve x^2 - c x - Kw = 0, and you get [H+] = 1.05e-7 M, pH 6.98. About 90% of the H+ comes from water.\n\nSave this for your next chemistry exam.\n\n#chemistry #physicalchemistry #pH #acidsandbases #stem #science #examprep #math",
 "cover_at": 1.0,
 "hook": "Exam question: pH of 10⁻⁸ M HCl. The answer 8 is wrong.",
 "sub": "Water changes the answer.",
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "The textbook shortcut: HCl is a strong acid, so $[\\mathrm{H^+}] = 10^{-8}$ M, and pH is eight.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "e1",
     "tex": [
      "\\mathrm{pH}",
      "=",
      "-\\log_{10}(10^{-8})",
      "=",
      "8"
     ],
     "size": 62,
     "at": [
      0,
      4.2
     ],
     "colors": {
      "4": "red"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "But pH 8 is basic. Adding acid to water can never make it basic. Something's wrong.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "numberline",
     "name": "nl",
     "range": [
      0,
      14,
      2
     ],
     "length": 7.6,
     "numbers": true,
     "at": [
      0,
      1.4
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "dot",
     "name": "d8",
     "on": "nl",
     "at": [
      8,
      0
     ],
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "make": "pointer",
     "name": "p8",
     "to": "d8",
     "text": "basic?",
     "side": "up",
     "buff": 1.0,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "make": "dot",
     "name": "d7",
     "on": "nl",
     "at": [
      7,
      0
     ],
     "color": "dim"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "What we forgot: water itself. At 25 °C it always keeps this product fixed, which gives $10^{-7}$ M of each ion.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "kw",
     "tex": [
      "[\\mathrm{H^+}]",
      "[\\mathrm{OH^-}]",
      "=",
      "K_w",
      "=",
      "10^{-14}"
     ],
     "size": 60,
     "at": [
      0,
      4.6
     ],
     "colors": {
      "3": "yellow"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Now count charges. Positive H⁺ must balance negative Cl⁻ (10⁻⁸ M) plus OH⁻.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "cb",
     "tex": [
      "[\\mathrm{H^+}]",
      "=",
      "c",
      "+",
      "\\frac{K_w}{[\\mathrm{H^+}]}"
     ],
     "size": 68,
     "next_to": "kw",
     "buff": 0.6,
     "colors": {
      "2": "blue",
      "4": "teal"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Call $x = [\\mathrm{H^+}]$ and multiply through by $x$. It's a quadratic.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "q",
     "tex": [
      "x^2",
      "-",
      "c\\,x",
      "-",
      "K_w",
      "=",
      "0"
     ],
     "size": 68,
     "next_to": "cb",
     "buff": 0.6
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Solve it with $c = 10^{-8}$ and $K_w = 10^{-14}$: $x \\approx 1.05\\times10^{-7}$ M.",
   "do": [
    {
     "sfx": "riser"
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "sol",
     "tex": [
      "x",
      "=",
      "\\frac{c+\\sqrt{c^2+4K_w}}{2}"
     ],
     "size": 64,
     "next_to": "q",
     "buff": 0.6
    },
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    },
    {
     "make": "box",
     "name": "bx",
     "around": "sol"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Where does that H⁺ come from? Almost all of it is the water. Units of $10^{-8}$ M:",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "tt",
     "tex": [
      "[\\mathrm{H^+}]\\ \\text{in units of } 10^{-8}\\,\\mathrm{M}"
     ],
     "size": 44,
     "color": "dim",
     "at": [
      0,
      5.7
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "bars",
     "name": "br",
     "values": [
      1.0,
      9.5,
      10.5
     ],
     "labels": [
      "acid",
      "water",
      "total"
     ],
     "colors": [
      "blue",
      "teal",
      "yellow"
     ],
     "max": 12,
     "step": 4,
     "size": [
      7.0,
      4.2
     ],
     "at": [
      0,
      3.0
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Water supplies about 90% of it. The pH comes out near 6.98: slightly acidic, as it must be.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "ph",
     "tex": [
      "\\mathrm{pH}",
      "\\approx",
      "6.98"
     ],
     "size": 96,
     "at": [
      0,
      -0.9
     ],
     "colors": {
      "2": "green"
     }
    },
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    },
    {
     "make": "box",
     "name": "bx2",
     "around": "ph",
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Ignoring water is fine for ordinary acids. It starts to fail as the concentration approaches $10^{-6}$ M and below.",
   "do": [
    {
     "hide": "bx2"
    },
    {
     "indicate": "ph",
     "color": "yellow"
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
